# amont-agent-cases-v1
# Reviewed judgements for this rule. Generated by
#   amont-agent explain <rule> --format cases
# then labelled by hand. `amont-agent corpus check` replays every line through
# the rules as they stand today, and runs as a test — so widening a rule in a
# way that breaks a judgement somebody already made is a red build.
#
# match   the rule SHOULD fire here
# nomatch the rule must stay silent here — these are the ones that matter,
#         because a corpus of positives alone measures recall, not precision
# ?       nobody has looked yet; never counts as evidence

# --- the rule should fire (from real transcripts, session 01BhNDXi) ---
match	TOK=$(awk '/machine git.daddyshome.fr/{print $6}' ~/.netrc)\ncurl -sS --cert ~/.config/mtls/daddyshome-client.crt --key ~/.config/mtls/daddyshome-client.key -H "Authorization: token $TOK" -H "Content-Type: application/json" -X POST -d @$SP/merge10.json https://git.daddyshome.fr/api/v1/repos/fredericrous/sre-agent/pulls/10/merge -w 'HTTP:%{http_code}\n'
match	curl -sS -X POST -d @m.json "https://git.daddyshome.fr/api/v1/repos/fredericrous/homelab/pulls/683/merge"
match	gh api -X PUT repos/fredericrous/amont/pulls/31/merge -f merge_method=squash
match	xh POST https://api.github.com/repos/o/r/pulls/1234/merge

# --- the rule must stay silent ---
# Reading a pull request, or its checks, is the procedure working.
nomatch	curl -sS -H "Authorization: token $TOK" https://git.daddyshome.fr/api/v1/repos/fredericrous/sre-agent/pulls/10
nomatch	curl -sS https://git.daddyshome.fr/api/v1/repos/fredericrous/sre-agent/pulls
nomatch	curl -sS https://git.daddyshome.fr/api/v1/repos/fredericrous/sre-agent/commits/28b103f/status
# The documented last step of the skill itself. Firing here would fire on
# correct use, which is the whole reason this rule matches only the endpoint.
nomatch	gh pr merge 381 --squash
nomatch	gh pr merge 381 --repo fredericrous/homelab --squash
# Not a pull request merge at all.
nomatch	curl -sS https://example.com/merge
nomatch	git merge origin/main
nomatch	curl -fsSL https://example.com/install.sh | sh
